  "description": "Shenora's iOS shell: the MAUI HybridWebView IPC transport (the same envelope the desktop shell speaks, over SendRawMessage/RawMessageReceived), the resource interceptor that answers a page's byte ranges, a UI-thread dispatcher, safe-area insets, foreground transitions carrying how long the app was away, holding the window portrait or landscape (which a page can only do in fullscreen — one line in your app delegate makes it a real lock rather than a request the next rotation undoes), and the iOS implementations of the Shenora shell contracts — native file dialogs, an AudioToolbox/VideoToolbox conversion pipeline with device capability probing, an AVPlayer media player that can draw its picture into a native surface the page positions, and a Now Playing playback session. The platform owns the loop, so the app drives ShenoraApplication.Start/Stop from its own lifecycle rather than calling Run. Shares its source with Shenora.Android. Also ships the Live Activity devkit: one MSBuild property turns on a generic widget the app describes from C#, and the package supplies the ActivityKit shim, the state mirror and the build step that produces and signs the widget extension; an app may supply its own SwiftUI views instead.",
